Yes, that's possible. But I don't think that was what the OP asked
for. Either way, I don't see any worthwhile benefit for such a change,
as long as it is just the color display effect alone as self purpose.

Though, one may add some new feature to the game where the color has
some meaning, e.g. the color might to a certain degree influence the
behaviour of monsters; it might scare monsters of complementary color,
make monsters of the same color more likely to be peaceful/tameable.

It could help to make the early Tourist game, which is one of the more
difficult classes, at least a bit easier (imagine a blue shirt calming
down soldier ants). But it would not be too powerful anyway, since any
character will strive to get body armor and a cloak, which would cover
the shirt and nullify its effect.

